<p><b>The World Congresses<p>
<p>
</b><p>
The World Congresses on project management are providing in-puts for new
inspirations, visions, clarity and concepts, and some innovative
computer-tailored tools to deal with the actual task. This trend is amply
reflected by the main themes of the most recent and future congresses:<p>
1967	Vienna (A)<p>
			"Network Methods"<p>
1966	Amsterdam (NL)<p>
			"Project Planning by Network Analysis"<p>
1972	Stockholm (S)<p>
			"Project Planning by Network Analysis"<p>
1974	Paris (F)<p>
			"Project Management in the Seventies"<p>
1976	Birmingham (UK)<p>
			"Project Implementation and Management"<p>
1979	Garmisch-Partenkirchen (FRG)<p>
			"The Problems of Project Management"<p>
1982	Copenhagen (DK)<p>
			"Project Management - Tools and Visions"<p>
1985	Rotterdam (NL)<p>
			"Clarify for the Nineties"<p>
1988	Glasgow, Scotland<p>
